* ============================================================
* INDEX TXN LMDB MAINTENANCE  (lane XIDX-TXN-01 M2 proof)
* ============================================================
* Purpose:
*   Prove LMDB index key maintenance happens INSIDE COMMIT on the
*   buffered (TABLE ON) path, with NO BUILDLMDB / REBUILD between the
*   mutation and the SEEK.
*
* Contrast with INDEX_X64 (index_v64_cdx_lmdb_smoke.dts):
*   that smoke mutates in immediate mode (TABLE OFF), which already works
*   today via the replaceFieldStored index hook. This script exercises the
*   TABLE ON -> REPLACE -> COMMIT path, which is the actual gap.
*
* Freshness is proven by SEEK (index-driven), NOT COUNT FOR (which scans
* the DBF and would pass even with a stale index).
*
* Falsifiable:
*   PRE-M1  : STEP 2 SEEK-new MISSES / SEEK-old still hits ; STEP 4 SEEK-deleted still hits.
*   POST-M1 : STEP 2 SEEK-new hits / SEEK-old misses ; STEP 4 SEEK-deleted misses.
*
* Non-destructive: operates on a disposable SANDBOX copy.
* ============================================================

SET TALK ON
ECHO ============================================================
ECHO INDEX TXN LMDB MAINTENANCE  (XIDX-TXN-01 M2)
ECHO ============================================================

* --- Self-bootstrap (mirror INDEX_X64 smoke) ---
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/SANDBOX
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/SANDBOX
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE students_txn_smoke CONFIRM

ECHO
ECHO --- MAKE DISPOSABLE COPY OF STUDENTS ---
USE students
COPY TO students_txn_smoke WITH SIDECARS OVERWRITE
CLOSE
USE students_txn_smoke
AREA
COUNT

ECHO
ECHO --- BUILD CDX + LMDB FOR THE COPY ---
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG SID
CDX ADDTAG LNAME
BUILDLMDB CLEAN YES
SET INDEX TO students_txn_smoke
SET ORDER TO TAG LNAME

* Enable transactional (in-COMMIT) index maintenance for this proof.
* Default is OFF (legacy batch rebuild); the gate steps below require it ON.
SET INDEXTXN ON

* ============================================================
ECHO
ECHO STEP 1 : baseline SEEK on a known key must hit
SEEK WHITE
TUP
ECHO EXPECT: SEEK WHITE found (landed row LNAME = WHITE)
ECHO ------------------------------------------------------------

* ============================================================
ECHO
ECHO STEP 2 (GATE) : BUFFERED REPLACE + COMMIT, then SEEK, NO rebuild
SEEK WHITE
TUP
TABLE ON
REPLACE LNAME WITH "ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED"
COMMIT
ECHO -- committed buffered key change; index must reflect it with no BUILDLMDB --
SEEK ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED
TUP
ECHO PRIMARY GATE -- unambiguous (unique sentinel key):
ECHO   EXPECT PASS (post-M1): SEEK ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED found, landed row LNAME = ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED
ECHO   EXPECT FAIL (pre-M1) : SEEK ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED Not found (index stale)
ECHO DUPLICATE-KEY PROOF (dup keys are allowed by design; composite base||recno8
ECHO keeps each row's entry distinct). Only rec 12 left the WHITE dup-set:
SEEK WHITE
TUP
ECHO   EXPECT (post-M1): SEEK WHITE still finds a *different* White row (e.g. rec 54),
ECHO   proving the incremental erase touched ONLY rec 12, not the other duplicates.
ECHO ------------------------------------------------------------

* ============================================================
ECHO
ECHO STEP 2b : ORDERED-MATERIALIZATION (browser / relation / join path)
ECHO Ordered nav (ERSATZ, SMARTBROWSE, REL ENUM/JOIN) materializes a recno vector
ECHO from the index. Under LNAME order the sentinel "ZZ_..." sorts LAST, so ordered
ECHO BOTTOM must land on it once the index is maintained (and after COMMIT called
ECHO reconcile_after_mutation to drop stale nav caches).
SET ORDER TO TAG LNAME
BOTTOM
TUP
ECHO EXPECT PASS (post-M1): ordered BOTTOM row LNAME = ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED (in index order)
ECHO EXPECT FAIL (pre-M1) : ordered BOTTOM = a real last name (sentinel absent from order)
ECHO ------------------------------------------------------------

* ============================================================
ECHO
ECHO STEP 3 : ROLLBACK leaves index (and DBF) untouched
SEEK MARTIN
TABLE ON
REPLACE LNAME WITH "ZZ_TXN_ROLLBACK"
ROLLBACK
SEEK ZZ_TXN_ROLLBACK
TUP
ECHO EXPECT PASS: SEEK ZZ_TXN_ROLLBACK NOT found (rolled back)
SEEK MARTIN
TUP
ECHO EXPECT PASS: SEEK MARTIN still found (unchanged)
ECHO ------------------------------------------------------------

* ============================================================
ECHO
ECHO STEP 4 (GATE) : BUFFERED DELETE + COMMIT removes key from index
ECHO Delete the STEP-2 sentinel record (rec 12) by recno, so the key is unique.
GOTO 12
TUP
SEEK ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED
TUP
ECHO   (post-M1: SEEK above should land on rec 12 = ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED)
GOTO 12
TABLE ON
DELETE
COMMIT
ECHO -- record deleted; CDX excludes deleted rows, so its key must leave the index --
SEEK ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED
TUP
ECHO EXPECT PASS (post-M1): SEEK ZZ_TXN_BUFFERED NOT found (deleted key erased)
ECHO (pre-M1: sentinel was never indexed, so this is Not found either way -
ECHO  STEP 2 is the discriminating gate; STEP 4 proves erase-on-delete post-M1.)
ECHO ------------------------------------------------------------

* ============================================================
ECHO
ECHO STEP 5 : negative control -- native CNX path is unchanged
ECHO (CNX still rebuilds at COMMIT; see INDEX_X32 / index_x32_inx_cnx_smoke.dts)
ECHO ------------------------------------------------------------

* --- Cleanup (mirror INDEX_X64 smoke) ---
ECHO
ECHO --- CLOSE + CLEANUP ---
* Restore ambient: this test flips the global SET INDEXTXN. Leave it OFF so it never
* leaves the ambient dirty for the next test (regression doctrine — sets/restores its
* own environment). This is also why INDEX_TXN stays out of the default suite.
SET INDEXTXN OFF
CLOSE
ERASE students_txn_smoke CONFIRM
ECHO Suggested manual cleanup if needed:
ECHO ERASE students_txn_smoke.dbf and students_txn_smoke.cdx / LMDB sidecars from SANDBOX paths.

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO INDEX TXN LMDB MAINTENANCE DONE  (score STEP 2 + STEP 4)
ECHO ============================================================
